  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a large saucepan of salted water to the boil for the ravioli. Cut the tomato into thin wedges. Crumble 1 stock cube into a heatproof jug, add half the tomato paste and 250ml (1 cup) boiling water and stir to dissolve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4221030/photos/large/prep_ingredients-f83a0980987f54af7adbc16df82ae1b2.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Start sauce: Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium-high heat. Add the red pesto and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4221031/photos/large/start_sauce-6d1bc7bc880299c493e0fca6f75eac26.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Finish sauce: Add the tomato stock to the pesto and bring to a simmer. Cook, stirring, for 3-4 mins until slightly thickened. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4221032/photos/large/cook_sauce-4b6f0867f5dff0bc7c68dd251207e003.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook ravioli: Meanwhile, cook the ravioli in the pan of boiling water for 3 mins or until al dente. Drain, then immediately add to the sauce and gently stir to combine (see Kitchen 101). Remove the pan from the heat. Taste, then season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4221033/photos/large/cook_ravioli-ce5e0187981408c2d01ba279aa5fb604.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Combine 1 tsp white wine vinegar and 1 tsp olive oil in a large bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the salad leaves and tomato and toss to combine. Divide the ravioli among bowls. Scatter over the hazelnuts and serve with the salad. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4221034/photos/large/serve_up-7d884efc120bfa73950d19ff52c7c61f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: The big rounds of ravioli look robust, but they actually love to be handled with care. Be gentle when draining and handling the cooked ravioli to ensure they don't break.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/4221035/photos/large/kitchen_101-793db0a007524b0e34abb1d7d1128e71.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
